                <pb facs="0579" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW (Peace)/11–447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in China
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-07T17:00:00-05:00">November 7, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1360. Urtel 2189, Nov. 4. Emb requested to
                    inform FonMin: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Dept has no objection China addressing identic notes Brit, Soviet and
                            US FonMins setting forth Chinese proposal for voting procedure in a Jap
                            peace conference as outlined by Chinese FonMin in conversation with
                            SecState Oct 9 nor does it object such notes being dispatched, as
                            suggested by Dr. Wang to you, before CFM
                            meeting.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Dept does not consider this subject appropriate for discussion
                            forthcoming CFM meeting in London. It is
                            not on agenda.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>In conveying above to Dr. Wang, please indicate to him this expression
                            Dept’s views does not constitute any change in US position.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
